    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my monstera deliciosa has been looking kinda rough lately. some of the lower leaves are turning a weird yellowish color and they feel a bit soft. i think i've been watering it about once a week but i'm not sure if that's too much or if it just needs more food? any idea what's going on?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowish yellow leaves, especially on the lower leaves, can be a sign of overwatering or root rot. Monsteras prefer moist soil but can be susceptible to waterlogged conditions. If you suspect the leaves are soft and mushy due to overwatering, consider reducing the frequency of watering to once every 10-14 days, allowing the top inch of soil to dry out between waterings.",
      "source": "target",
